'''Tom Newton''' (born March 8, 1954) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[running back]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) for six seasons with the [[New York Jets]] and two seasons for the [[Oakland Raiders]]. He played [[college football]] for the [[California Golden Bears football|California Golden Bears]].<ref name="stats">{{Cite web|url=https://www.profootballarchives.com/playern/newt01400.html|title = Tom Newton Stats - Pro Football Archives}}</ref> He finished his NFL career with a total of 772 yards and nine [[Touchdown|touchdowns]].<ref name="stats"></ref>

Newton was born in Carmel, [[Florida]],<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/N/NewtTo00.htm|title = Tom Newton Stats| website=[[Pro-Football-Reference.com]] }}</ref> and has one child, a daughter named Khalishia Newton.{{Cn|date=January 2025}}

