'''Tom Moriarty''' (born April 7, 1953) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[defensive back]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL). He played [[college football]] for the [[Bowling Green Falcons football|Bowling Green Falcons]]. Moriarty played in the NFL for the [[Atlanta Falcons]] from 1977 to 1979 and again in 1981 as well as playing one season with the [[Pittsburgh Steelers]] in 1980.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MoriTo20.htm |title=Tom Moriarty NFL Football Statistics |publisher=Pro-Football-Reference.com |accessdate=September 7, 2015}}</ref> He also played for the [[Michigan Panthers]] of the [[United States Football League]] (USFL).<ref>{{Cite news |author=Maxse, Joe |title=Whatever Happened To ... Tom Moriarty, former Benedictine and NFL football player |newspaper=[[The Plain Dealer]] |date=September 9, 2011 |url=http://highschoolsports.cleveland.com/news/article/-8481045927961141842/whatever-happened-to-tom-moriarty-former-benedictine-and-nfl-football-player/ |accessdate=September 7, 2015}}</ref>
